  <item>
    <title>14 创伤预警让我们更安全、更脆弱，还是更勇敢？｜箱里向外</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/67bc4f7705a90dfd0d87bfbc</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">67bc4f7705a90dfd0d87bfbc</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 24 Feb 2025 11:10:09 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>创伤预警（Trigger Warning）通常是视频、文字内容或活动开头的一段声明，用以提醒读者或参与者，接下来的内容涉及暴力、灾难等可能触发伤痛记忆的描述，可根据自身情况决定继续或暂停接收信息。</span></p><span></span><p><span>作为系统性暴力的承受者，女性、性少数、残障等进步社群对创伤预警的重视由来已久，但关于是否应该使用、应该在何时使用的争议一直没有停止。本期播客，我们将从女性主义的角度出发，结合自己身处社群的感受，讨论对这个问题的不同观点和实践。</span></p><span></span><p><span>【播客内容】</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="58">00:58</a> 创伤预警，“通向无障碍的祝祷词”</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="371">06:11</a> 教学领域的创伤预警，带来内容审查还是教育公平？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="988">16:28</a> 网络女性主义社群建设另类空间的实践</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1298">21:38</a> “上路吧，现在要讨论一些让人不舒服的东西了”</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1738">28:58</a> 对创伤预警的反思：没有真正的安全</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1974">32:54</a> 安全空间是稀缺资源</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2184">36:24</a> 从安全空间到勇敢空间</span></p><span></span><p><span>相关资料：</span></p><span></span><p><span>关于罗克珊·盖伊《饥饿》的播客：</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/66f277e12adfe48b83113311" data-url="https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/66f277e12adfe48b83113311"><span>www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>戏剧《奴隶游戏（Slave Play）》：</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.douban.com/location/drama/30426316/" data-url="https://www.douban.com/location/drama/30426316/"><span>www.douban.com</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>Kyrölä, Kata. 2018. Negotiating Vulnerability in the Trigger Warning Debates</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.manchesteropenhive.com/downloadpdf/9781526133113/9781526133113.00007.pdf" data-url="https://www.manchesteropenhive.com/downloadpdf/9781526133113/9781526133113.00007.pdf"><span>www.manchesteropenhive.com</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>Sara Ahmed. 2014. Feminist Hurt/Feminism Hurts</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://feministkilljoys.com/2014/07/21/feminist-hurtfeminism-hurts/" data-url="https://feministkilljoys.com/2014/07/21/feminist-hurtfeminism-hurts/"><span>feministkilljoys.com</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>Roxane Gay. 2012. The Illusion of Safety/The Safety of Illusion</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://uwm.edu/cultures-communities/wp-content/uploads/sites/219/2018/10/The-Illusion-Of-Safety-The-Safety-Of-Illusion.pdf" data-url="https://uwm.edu/cultures-communities/wp-content/uploads/sites/219/2018/10/The-Illusion-Of-Safety-The-Safety-Of-Illusion.pdf"><span>uwm.edu</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>Hudson, James and Kathrine McKittrick. 2014. The Geographies of Blackness and Anti-Blackness: An Interview with Katherine McKittrick</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.pdcnet.org/85257989005F24CA/file/0B6C499CA1675D4FC1257D6A0061578B/$FILE/clrjames_2014_0020_0001_0237_0244.pdf" data-url="https://www.pdcnet.org/85257989005F24CA/file/0B6C499CA1675D4FC1257D6A0061578B/$FILE/clrjames_2014_0020_0001_0237_0244.pdf"><span>www.pdcnet.org$FILE/clrjames_2014_0020_0001_0237_0244.pdf</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>【本期参与】</span></p><span></span><p><span>主播：小饼干、柠檬</span></p><span></span><p><span>剪辑：宇宙少女</span></p><span></span><p><span>【关于我们】</span></p><span></span><p><span>箱里向外：女性主义文化心理类播客。一群女人的闲聊、观影、阅读、思考。</span></p><span></span><p><span>公众号、小红书同名。</span></p>]]></description>
    <enclosure url="https://media.xyzcdn.net/6684c47c53526fced02dd69f/lpPoYB_JHD573YNPF6my1oQNeeuq.m4a" length="40425380" type="audio/mp4"/>
    <itunes:duration>00:41:37</itunes:duration>
    <itunes:image href="https://image.xyzcdn.net/Ft09JPLLO_X8v3TIIMl8i01lTy6s.jpg"/>
    <itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>13 “女权神话”《好东西》，让愤怒的年轻女性找到出口｜箱里向外</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/67552f6dbdb9877a97274c66</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">67552f6dbdb9877a97274c66</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 08 Dec 2024 05:53:37 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>作为一部女权商业喜剧片，《好东西》不仅取得了票房上的成功，也在网络上的年轻女权社群中受到广泛欢迎。</span></p><span></span><p><span>《好东西》塑造了一个共同育儿的女性乌托邦，同时嵌入了各种社交媒体上流行的女权话题，比如上野千鹤子。同为熟悉这些话题的“年轻女权主义者”，我们像是被电影做了一场心灵按摩，既为“女权”这个词能出现在中国荧幕而激动，也不时因为看到生活中“熟悉的配方”而会心一笑，乃至二刷、三刷之后，都觉得很感动。</span></p><span></span><p><span>另一方面，电影也面临“说教”“悬浮”的批评。我们试图不局限于对电影本身的褒贬，而更多地从“我们为什么喜欢这部电影”出发，讨论它所反映和引发的文化现象，并进一步看国内女权社群当下的处境和文化实践。</span></p><span></span><p><span>【播客内容】</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="328">05:28</a> 影片的优点</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="826">13:46</a> “女权表演艺术家”的巧妙设置</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1207">20:07</a> “很酷的邻居姐姐帮忙带孩子”——怎么看电影里的女性乌托邦？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1539">25:39</a> 王铁梅的经历映射了女权在中国的转型</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1760">29:20</a> 女权主义影视创作的责任感；呈现房间里的大象</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2115">35:15</a> 除了重复流行文化符号，女权电影有没有可能设置新的议程？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3249">54:09</a> 将电影作为文化现象，观察国内的女权讨论和实践</span></p><span></span><p><span>【本期参与】</span></p><span></span><p><span>主播：犀牛、薄荷、橘子</span></p><span></span><p><span>剪辑：宇宙少女</span></p><span></span><p><span>【关于我们】</span></p><span></span><p><span>箱里向外：女性主义文化心理类播客。一群女人的闲聊、观影、阅读、思考。</span></p><span></span><p><span>公众号、小红书同名。</span></p>]]></description>
    <enclosure url="https://media.xyzcdn.net/lkj_dz767aP5oFcenXN61bl_plY9.m4a" length="57479756" type="audio/mp4"/>
    <itunes:duration>00:59:10</itunes:duration>
